{"name":"Biking Trail","hex":"#c3c0b1","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"biking","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The act, process, or sport of riding a bike .","The act, process, or sport of riding a bicycle."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["present participle and gerund of bike"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/biking"},{"term":"trail","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To follow behind (someone or something); to tail (someone or something).","To drag (something) behind on the ground."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The track or indication marking the route followed by something that has passed, such as the footprints of animal on land or the contrail of an airplane in the sky.","A route for travel over land, especially a narrow, unpaved pathway for use by hikers, horseback riders, etc."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/trail"}],"entries":[{"title":"Cycling","blocks":[{"text":"Cycling, also known as bicycling or biking, is the activity of riding a bicycle or other types of pedal-driven human-powered vehicles such as balance bikes, unicycles, tricycles, and quadricycles. Cycling is practised around the world for purposes including transport, recreation, exercise, and competitive sport."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d0/Cycliste_%C3%A0_place_d%27Italie-Paris_crop.jpg/330px-Cycliste_%C3%A0_place_d%27Italie-Paris_crop.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cycling"},{"title":"Trail","blocks":[{"text":"A trail, also known as a path or track, is a dirt road or a small paved road, usually through an undeveloped natural area, that is designed primarily for use by pedestrians, equestrians and non-motorized vehicles, although occasionally some off-roading motor vehicles may also use it. In the United Kingdom and Ireland, footpath or hiking trail is the preferred term. However, it is sometimes applied to highways in North America. In the United States, the term was historically used to describe the westward expansion trails, which are land routes into or through wildness regions of the American West used by explorers and migrants."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b0/Trail_between_two_fields_%28Slovenia%2C_Selo_pri_Mirni%29.jpg/330px-Trail_between_two_fields_%28Slovenia%2C_Selo_pri_Mirni%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Trail"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/02/Two_siblings_on_their_way_home_after_school.jpg/500px-Two_siblings_on_their_way_home_after_school.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/02/Two_siblings_on_their_way_home_after_school.jpg/1280px-Two_siblings_on_their_way_home_after_school.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/02/Two_siblings_on_their_way_home_after_school.jpg/500px-Two_siblings_on_their_way_home_after_school.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Children riding a bike in Ghana","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ATwo_siblings_on_their_way_home_after_school.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0f/Cycling_kit_full_body.jpg/500px-Cycling_kit_full_body.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0f/Cycling_kit_full_body.jpg/1280px-Cycling_kit_full_body.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0f/Cycling_kit_full_body.jpg/500px-Cycling_kit_full_body.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbn